        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: merge sanity 133f and 133g",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: merge sanity 133f and 133g\n\nsanity tests 133f (client) and 133g (server) each run\nbadarea_io over the proc files and then end with a\ncleanup/setup remount, because the writes can leave\ntunables set to garbage.  The test bodies take a few\nseconds; the remount is 60 to 150 seconds each.\n\nFold the server part into 133f so one remount follows\nboth the client and server writes, and remove 133g.  If\nthe MDS or OST is nodsh only the server part is skipped.\nA badarea_io failure no longer ends the test, so the\nserver part and the remount still run after it.\n\nMeasured on a single-node rocky9 setup, 133f and 133g\ntook 47 s each, and the merged 133f takes 64 s.  In CI\n133g averages 207 s over 14479 runs per 30 days.\n\n133g rarely fails: 9 failed sessions out of about 78000\nsuite runs in 90 days (11 failures, all on 4 in-flight\nchanges).  Its Maloo history ends with this change, and\na standalone ONLY=133f now also runs the server part.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=133f\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Icea891e15e1419b949c4b4621c1ef5cdc0a6b899\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
